    498→## The scheduler
    …
    500→Neco uses [sco](https://github.com/tidwall/sco), which is a fair and
    501→deterministic scheduler. This means that no coroutine takes priority over
    502→another and that all concurrent operations will reproduce in an expected order.
    504→### Fast context switching
    …
    511→### Thread local runtime
    …
    513→There can be no more than one scheduler per thread.
    523→_Pthread utilties such as `pthread_mutex_t` and `pthread_cond_t` do not work very well in coroutines._
